%   data: {"dataType":"text","outputData":{"text":" <strong>isreal<\/strong> - Determine whether array uses complex storage\n    This MATLAB function returns logical 1 (true) when numeric array A does\n    not have an imaginary part, and logical 0 (false) otherwise.\n\n    Syntax\n      tf = <strong>isreal<\/strong>(A)\n\n    Input Arguments\n      <a href=\"matlab:web('C:\\Program Files\\MATLAB\\R2025b\\help\/matlab\/ref\/double.isreal.html#bt4oz5d-1-A')\">A<\/a> - Input array\n        scalar | vector | matrix | multidimensional array\n\n    Examples\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/DetermineWhetherMatrixContainsAllRealValuesExample')\">Determine Whether Matrix Contains All Real Values<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/DefineComplexNumberwithZeroValuedImaginaryPartExample')\">Define Complex Number with Zero-Valued Imaginary Part<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/ComputationResultinginZeroValuedImaginaryPartExample')\">Computation Resulting in Zero-Valued Imaginary Part<\/a>\n      <a href=\"matlab:openExample('matlab\/FindRealElementsinCellArrayExample')\">Find Real Elements in Cell Array<\/a>\n\n    See also <a href=\"matlab:help complex -displayBanner\">complex<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help isnumeric -displayBanner\">isnumeric<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help isnan -displayBanner\">isnan<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help isprime -displayBanner\">isprime<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help isfinite -displayBanner\">isfinite<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help isinf -displayBanner\">isinf<\/a>, <a href=\"matlab:help isa -displayBanner\">isa<\/a>\n\n    Introduced in MATLAB before R2006a\n    <a href=\"matlab:doc isreal\">Documentation for isreal<\/a>\n\n","truncated":false}}
